+              <dd pn="section-3.2-6.10.1.8">
+                <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-6.10.1.8.1">Unspecified reason not covered by other failure codes.</t>
+                <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-6.10.1.8.2">The failure message of last resort.</t>
+              </dd>
+            </dl>
+          </dd>
+        </dl>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-7">The following failure response messages are only used by the Label
+Range message.</t>
+        <dl newline="false" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-3.2-8">
+          <dt pn="section-3.2-8.1">29:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-3.2-8.2">Cannot support requested VPI range.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-3.2-8.3">30:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-3.2-8.4">Cannot support requested VCI range on all requested VPIs.</dd>
+        </dl>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-9">The following failure response messages are only used by the Set
+Transmit Cell Rate function of the Port Management
+message.</t>
+        <dl newline="false" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-3.2-10">
+          <dt pn="section-3.2-10.1">31:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-3.2-10.2">The transmit cell rate of this output port cannot be changed.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-3.2-10.3">32:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-3.2-10.4">Requested transmit cell rate out of range for this output
+port.</dd>
+        </dl>
+      </section>
